title: Hash-of-scalar fields validate nothing -- ResourceRequirements limits accepts
  cpu => banana
updated: 2026-08-31T19:04:17Z
---

The k8s DSL form { Str => 1 } maps to a bare HashRef with NO inner
constraint (lib/IO/K8s/Resource.pm:236, comment: "Use plain HashRef
without inner constraint - K8s has nested hashes"). Neither the key nor
the value type is checked.

Repro (measured):

  ResourceRequirements->new(limits => { cpu => "banana" })
  --> constructs, and to_json emits {"limits":{"cpu":"banana"}}

Upstream types limits/requests as map[ResourceName]Quantity. So the
most-used quantity-carrying fields in the whole distribution validate
nothing, while the 30 fields typed Quantity (karr #52) are strict. The
error only surfaces at the API server -- exactly the fail-open shape the
house line rejects (karr #37/#39).

Scope: the { Str => 1 } form appears ~215 times across lib/. Not all of
them carry Quantities (many are genuinely opaque string maps, e.g.
labels/annotations), so this is NOT a mass sed -- the work is deciding
which fields have a real inner type upstream and typing only those.

Fix sketch: add a hash-of-scalar-type form to the k8s DSL, e.g.
{ Quantity => 1 }, carried through the attribute registry and the
serializer the same way the existing hash-of-objects form is; then
retype the fields whose upstream schema names a concrete value type.
DSL + registry change, not a Types.pm change.

Note this reframes karr #52: its headline impact ("30 Quantity fields")
understates the real exposure, because the fields users touch most
(ResourceRequirements requests/limits) were never type-checked at all.

Found by the types lane while implementing karr #52 (repro verified by
the orchestrating agent).
Lane: decision on scope first, then io-k8s-worker, then io-k8s-test-writer.

2026-08-31 04:07 Scope decision: built the { Quantity => 1 } (and Int/Num/Bool/Time/IntOrStr) DSL mechanism and retyped the fields I could verify with high confidence as upstream map[ResourceName]Quantity (ResourceRequirements/VolumeResourceRequirements limits+requests, NodeStatus capacity/allocatable, ResourceQuota hard/used, LimitRangeItem 5 fields, PV(C) capacity/allocatedResources, DRA BasicDevice v1alpha3 capacity + CapacityRequirements requests). Left genuinely-opaque maps as { Str => 1 } (labels/annotations/fieldsV1, and PVCStatus.allocatedResourceStatuses which is a status enum, not Quantity). Did NOT blanket-retype the other ~200 { Str => 1 } sites -- most are legitimately opaque; a wrong retype would be a new fail-closed-on-valid-data bug. Fixed in 95d579fa, test t/64; t/42 synthesizer updated. Full suite green (4112).
